INT. GRAIN SILO, HEAVY BOMBER BASE - NIGHT

A hollow concrete cylinder smelling of dust and old wheat. A rope ladder dangles from a hatch. Moonlight falls through the hatch in a pale coin on the floor.

Three men huddle around a hurricane lamp. LIEUTENANT CASIMIR WOJCIK-ASANTE (30s, flight jacket, no cap) sits on an overturned drum. SERGEANT TIBERIUS HALLORAN-OKORO (40s, a bandaged hand) cleans a pistol. YOUNG PRIVATE JONAH ABERNATHY-LIU (19, a radio on his lap) fiddles with its dials.

CASIMIR
How long since the last patrol?

TIBERIUS
Two hours.

CASIMIR
Nothing on the radio?

JONAH
Static, sir. Just static.

CASIMIR
Try the emergency band.

JONAH
I've tried it.

CASIMIR
Try it again.

Jonah turns the dial. Static rises, falls. A fragment of music, dance-band, swells and fades.

TIBERIUS
That's Berlin.

CASIMIR
That's Brussels.

TIBERIUS
It's Berlin.

CASIMIR
Sergeant, I have flown over both.

TIBERIUS
Sir, I have been bombed by both.

CASIMIR
(a dry smile)
Then we are experts.

JONAH
Sir, may I ask something?

CASIMIR
You may.

JONAH
Are we going to be all right?

Tiberius stops cleaning the pistol. Casimir leans back until his drum creaks.

CASIMIR
Private, the war ends. Whether we end with it is a matter of arithmetic.

JONAH
Arithmetic?

TIBERIUS
He means luck.

CASIMIR
I mean luck with decimals.

Jonah laughs, small and surprised. Tiberius cracks a smile. For a moment all three men are grinning in the lamplight like boys in a treehouse.

Then the grin falters. Overhead, very faint, a droning begins. It swells. The lamp flame trembles. Tiberius lowers the pistol, Casimir springs to his feet, and Jonah clutches the radio to his chest, all three staring up at the coin of moonlight as the hatch rattles on its hinges.

TIBERIUS
Ours.

CASIMIR
You're sure?

TIBERIUS
Listen to the engines.

They listen. The drone passes directly overhead. It's steady. Unhurried. It fades toward the east.

JONAH
(whisper)
Ours.

CASIMIR
Ours.

They sit down again, slowly. No one speaks. Tiberius resumes cleaning the pistol. Jonah turns the dial back to the dance band, very low.
